                                "sense_id": "8a6a22e5-cc82-300f-8796-2fd92033a771",
                                "text": "GRammar is the Art of Letters, as the Greek word γράμμα (whence it is dervived) imports : Of Letters are made Syllables, of Syllables Words, and by the coagmentation of letters, ſyllables , and words , is fram’d Sermocination of Speech, which is one of the eminentſt Prærogatives of Mankind above all other ſublunary Cretures ; for though others (as ſom volatils) by art, and hardſhip are brought to utter ſom broken words, yet they underſtand not what they ſpeak, becauſe they are deſtitut of the faculty of Reſon, Man onely being the child of Reſon."
